# jextract argument file: CPython's version-specific (non-Stable-ABI) API, as
# declared by the Python 3.14 headers. Generates com.example.ffm.python.capi.py314
# (task jextractCPython314), which the build refuses to generate from any other
# version's headers.
#
# None of these exist before 3.14: only call them after checking the loaded
# libpython's Py_Version (internal.ApiLevel). As with cpython312.symbols, only add
# symbols whose declarations are unchanged in every later supported version;
# PyConfig_Get is identical in 3.14 and 3.15.

# PEP 741: read the interpreter's configuration by name; a new reference.
# Replaces the Py_Get*() path functions, deprecated in 3.13 and removed from the
# 3.15 headers.
--include-function PyConfig_Get
